    <diagram id="p1" name="Part 1: game information, server and types">
        <mxGraphModel dx="1736" dy="1146" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
            <root>
                <mxCell id="0"/>
                <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
                <mxCell id="p1-note" value="&lt;b&gt;Part 1: game information, server and types&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;+ public (props, exports), - private, / computed and getters, «emit» events. The four modules live in src/shared/. currentGame is a plain reactive() object and keeps gameId, myPlayerId and mySecretKey in sessionStorage. api.removePlayer does both leaving and kicking: DELETE /api/games/{id}/players/{playerToRemove}. api.keepUpToDate opens the live connection (STOMP over SockJS), asks the server for the whole game again on every (re)connect and every 6 s, and returns a stop function. Generated from &lt;code&gt;frontend-graph.md&lt;/code&gt;." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;spacing=4;" parent="1" vertex="1"><mxGeometry y="10" width="820" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
